WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
One request, typed the way a client actually writes it.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
"I need a landing page for Fernwood Dental Studio, a family dental clinic in Victoria —

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
and an automation that emails me whenever someone submits the booking form
and adds them to a Google Sheet."

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Two products in one sentence. The front person hires its team and says so.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Front person. Builder. Delivery orchestrator. Each hire shown as it completes.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Five seconds in, the landing page is live at a public address and serving.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The automation half then takes over, and the page keeps narrating it.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Integrator working. Workflow provisioner working. Quality check verifying.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Two minutes in: "Your automation is ready. Download the file from the Files
list on this page and import it into your n8n to run it."

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Two deliverables from one sentence. The page is public; the workflow is a file.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Every attempt is metered against a hard three-cent ceiling per job,
and the receipt names what was spent.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
What this does not show: the model's reasoning, a success rate,
or the workflow running inside the client's own n8n.
